{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-73340","model_call":28,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q798"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q798"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_06_1778472344#2_2688091675","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q798","rank":8,"snippet":"whistleblowers will be killed. This is even happening at the state level — the Wisconsin legislature convened under the cover of night to pass a bill banning the Center for Investigative Journalism from the University of Wisconsin campus, directly intruding on a free press’ right to public documents. Download This didn’t all just happen overnight. After the passage of the Patriot Act in 2001, our rights to privacy as citizens were signed away. Sen. Russ <cover>Feingold (D-WI) was the only senator who voted no to the bill that gave massive new powers to the DOJ. Sen. Mary Landrieu (D-LA) didn’t vote yes or no. The House vote for the 2001 bill was also pretty one-sided - the Patriot Act passed 357-66. </cover>When it came up for reauthorization in 2006, the Senate passed it 89-10 (there were several who voted yes in 2001 and no in 2006) and the house passed it 280-138.\" , \"start_char\": 1497.000000 , \"title\": \"\" , \"url\": \"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/carl-gibson/how-to-win-the-war-on-ter_b_3406966.html\" }"},"time":16},"model_calls":28,"document_judgments":21,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
