{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-73340","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q802"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q802"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1431644496#15_2749717303","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q802","rank":3,"snippet":", \"headings\": \" H.R. 514, PATRIOT Act Extension Summary: Legislative Background: “Roving Wiretaps” Access to Business Records and Tangible Things “Lone Wolf” Alternative Extensions Introduced in the 112th Congress: Sen. Feinstein - S.289 Sen. Leahy - S.193 Sen. McConnell – S. 291 Key Roll Call Votes: \" , \"segment\": \"Passed 251-174, House Vote 627, 12/14/05 The Intelligence Reform and Terrorism Prevention Act of 2004, which passed in December 2004, included the so-called “lone wolf” provision. Key Roll Call Votes: Final Senate Passage: Passed 89-2, Senate Vote 216, 12/8/04 Final House Passage: Passed 336-75, House Vote 544, 12/7/04 The initial USA <cover>PATRIOT Act was signed into law in October 2001. Key Roll Call Votes: Final Senate Passage: Passed 98-1, Senate Vote 313, 10/25/01 Final House Passage: Passed 357-66, </cover>House Vote 398, 10/24/01 DPC\" , \"start_char\": 8852.000000 , \"title\": \"H.R. 514, PATRIOT Act Extension\" , \"url\": \"http://www.dpc.senate.gov/dpcdoc.cfm?doc_name=lb-112-1-7\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1431644496#15_2749717303","rank":3,"relevance":3}]},"time":7},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":23,"relevance_3":16,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
